                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91b01ffd-3987-4a8f-9be3-da403798616b",
                                                "sense_id": "87ca99d1-4807-397a-9466-e1a043022999",
                                                "text": "Slightly sunken brown cankers of variable size and shape affect stem parts primarily below the soil line."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4477c2d3-d1a9-39b9-824e-cb497feb404a",
                                        "entry_id": "ecfa392c-af76-3774-a7d8-3efb21576e3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A worm or grub that destroys plant buds or leaves; cankerworm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77e25afe-ea4e-49e5-b742-df07fb40bde0",
                                                "sense_id": "4477c2d3-d1a9-39b9-824e-cb497feb404a",
                                                "text": "loathsome canker lives in sweetest bud[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "054b72a8-dddb-3c39-817c-fbcdca001b45",
                                        "entry_id": "ecfa392c-af76-3774-a7d8-3efb21576e3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A corroding or sloughing ulcer; especially a spreading gangrenous ulcer or collection of ulcers in or about the mouth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9193658-241a-347b-818e-bf6720418e32",
                                        "entry_id": "ecfa392c-af76-3774-a7d8-3efb21576e3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything which corrodes, corrupts, or destroys."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c63424c-4b80-4049-abce-be4df01f515f",
                                                "sense_id": "c9193658-241a-347b-818e-bf6720418e32",
                                                "text": "the cankers of envy and faction"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "636d63b7-aa99-48ca-866d-6a2a34aa7bdc",
                                                "sense_id": "c9193658-241a-347b-818e-bf6720418e32",
                                                "text": "There’s canker at the root, your seed\nDenies the blessing of the sun,\nThe light essential to your need.\nYour hopes are murdered and undone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6fc86a6-1058-3e3c-8b0c-7139435caf5e",
                                        "entry_id": "ecfa392c-af76-3774-a7d8-3efb21576e3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of wild rose; the dog rose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51864fa0-aca8-48ea-a907-300e5c2a40d4",
                                                "sense_id": "a6fc86a6-1058-3e3c-8b0c-7139435caf5e",
                                                "text": "To put down Richard, that ſweet louely Roſe,\nAnd plant this thorne, this canker Bullingbrooke?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "baa6d8a1-0018-3d3b-9cd9-012c289a6c77",
                                        "entry_id": "ecfa392c-af76-3774-a7d8-3efb21576e3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An obstinate and often incurable disease of a horse's foot, characterized by separation of the horny portion and the development of fungoid growths. Usually resulting from neglected thrush."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5521fee-b77a-3d2c-8ed0-0b44c5bac17f",
                                        "entry_id": "ecfa392c-af76-3774-a7d8-3efb21576e3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An avian disease affecting doves, poultry, parrots and birds of prey, caused by Trichomonas gallinae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4bf138b2-c23e-30d6-8e23-7f4fa7b6cfc8",
                                        "entry_id": "ecfa392c-af76-3774-a7d8-3efb21576e3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crab."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Cornwall",
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff7cac60-5f0c-4bcf-a878-02fed155f564",
                                                "sense_id": "4bf138b2-c23e-30d6-8e23-7f4fa7b6cfc8",
                                                "text": "This Caſtoꝛ liueth by water and lande, he loueth to feede vpon Crabbes and Cankers of the Sea."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c920bcb6-2445-495a-b096-e80fbbef8074",
                                                "sense_id": "4bf138b2-c23e-30d6-8e23-7f4fa7b6cfc8",
                                                "text": "It is this power of active motion which has obtained it a local name in the West of Cornwall, where, as crabs in general are termed \"cankers,\" this species is distinguished by the name of \"flying canker.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "canker",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03121164-6f4b-30d6-b758-cae71275a084",
                                        "entry_id": "c94d565c-f9f1-3477-9afe-f8bbc0263b36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To affect as a canker; to eat away; to corrode; to consume."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45d41e74-a77c-4d6d-a3f4-9eb4d2d82cce",
                                                "sense_id": "03121164-6f4b-30d6-b758-cae71275a084",
                                                "text": "Still onward winds the dreary way; / I with it; for I long to prove / No lapse of moons can canker Love, / Whatever fickle tongues may say."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e1ae18a-af45-38b0-bb90-fa41315296a8",
                                        "entry_id": "c94d565c-f9f1-3477-9afe-f8bbc0263b36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To infect or pollute; to corrupt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df532bcc-0961-3156-abe0-8322a28533d2",
                                        "entry_id": "c94d565c-f9f1-3477-9afe-f8bbc0263b36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To waste away, grow rusty, or be oxidized, as a mineral."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7393331c-4ed6-3750-a459-6b3269495dd8",
                                        "entry_id": "c94d565c-f9f1-3477-9afe-f8bbc0263b36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be or become diseased, or as if diseased, with canker; to grow corrupt; to become venomous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d698eab-1425-4faa-843c-82698696fcfe",
                                                "sense_id": "7393331c-4ed6-3750-a459-6b3269495dd8",
                                                "text": "as with age his body uglier grows,\nSo his mind cankers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e14f486-d527-4271-9491-76fba807b5c8",
                                                "sense_id": "7393331c-4ed6-3750-a459-6b3269495dd8",
                                                "text": "[…] the road, always in bad condition, was edged with dog roses that scratched the paint. Blossom after blossom crept past them, draggled by the ungenial year: some had cankered, others would never unfold:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c73237ce-8640-45b8-97da-72429c4edb7a",
                        "source_entry_id": "64c37780-286c-3647-b21a-8c8649fa6fe1",
